qcom-va-driver (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Provide and conflict with libva-v4l2 to support full package replacement
    while preserving dependencies on the old package name.

 -- Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:22:57 +0800

qcom-va-driver (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the project and package to qcom-va-driver, replacing libva-v4l2
    without a transitional package and preserving driver names and session
    configuration paths.
  * Add AV1 Main 8/10-bit decoding on supported Iris devices.
  * Fix HEVC Main10 format handling, Chromium PRIME1 surface imports and
    decoder error recovery; bound CAPTURE buffer memory usage.
  * Replace FastCV with selectable CDSP/Vulkan video processing for scaling,
    cropping, rotation, NV12/P010 conversion and RGB overlay composition.
  * Add Vulkan HDR10-to-SDR tone mapping. Enable Vulkan video processing in
    Debian packages while keeping CDSP disabled.
  * Make GPU surface copying optional and improve VPP allocation fallback.
  * Generate pkg.conf for SC8280XP release and test repositories in CI.

 -- Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:50:01 +0800

